# Line endings.
#
# Every source file here is LF, but Git on Windows defaults to checking files
# out as CRLF — which is where the wall of "LF will be replaced by CRLF"
# warnings on the first commit came from. Left alone it is mostly cosmetic,
# until the day this is cloned onto a second machine and the first save
# rewrites every line of every file into one enormous whitespace diff.
#
# `eol=lf` pins both sides: LF in the repository and LF in the working tree,
# on every platform. Node, Vite, tsx and Rust are all indifferent to which,
# so there is no reason to let it vary.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never line-ending-process these — Git's binary detection is good, but an
# icon mangled by a newline substitution is a corrupt file that still looks
# like a valid path in a diff.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.exe binary
